{"availability":"available","full":"cloudflare/vinext","name":"vinext","description":"Vite plugin that reimplements the Next.js API surface — deploy anywhere","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":9087,"forks":429,"created":"2026-02-24T05:07:41Z","updated":"2026-10-02T16:00:41Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://vinext.dev","topics":[],"demo":"https://app-router-playground.vinext.workers.dev/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T21:34:29.651Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T21:34:29.651Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T21:34:29.651Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:19:34.822Z","stars":9084,"forks":428},{"at":"2026-10-04T21:34:29.651Z","stars":9087,"forks":429}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:36.535Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Under active development. vinext supports substantial Next.js applications today, but it is not yet a drop-in replacement for every application or production workload. Expect compatibility gaps, especially in newer App Router features, and evaluate it against your own application before adopting it.","vinext reimplements the Next.js API surface on Vite rather than consuming next build output. It supports both the App Router and Pages Router, React Server Components, Server Actions, middleware, route handlers, ISR, static export, and the most commonly used next/ modules. Cloudflare Workers has the deepest integration; Node.js and other platforms are available with different levels of support.","Vite has become the default build tool for modern web frameworks — fast HMR, a clean plugin API, native ESM, and a growing ecosystem. With @vitejs/plugin-rsc adding React Server Components support, it's now possible to build a full RSC framework on Vite."],"features":["OpenNext — adapts next build output for AWS, Cloudflare, and other platforms. OpenNext has been around much longer than vinext, is more mature, and covers mo